<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p><b>Effective date:</b> November 11, 2026</p>

<p>
  This Privacy Policy explains what information <b>0stakes</b> ("we", "us", "our"), the
  website at <a href="https://0stakes.com">0stakes.com</a>, collects, how it is used, and the
  choices you have. 0stakes is a free practice site for casino table games. There is no
  real-money gambling. You can play every game without an account. An optional account
  keeps a free, play-money chip balance across games and devices.
</p>

<h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
<p><b>Information you give us</b></p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Feedback form:</b> if you use our <a href="/feedback/">feedback form</a>, we receive your message, the topic you choose, the page you were on, and your email address only if you choose to provide it.</li>
  <li><b>Optional account:</b> if you create an account, we collect your email address, a username you choose, and a password (stored only as a salted hash by our authentication provider, never in readable form). We also store your chip balance and a ledger of chip changes: signup and daily bonuses, refills, and the net win or loss of each game session, with the game name and time.</li>
  <li><b>Email contact:</b> if you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you include in your message.</li>
  <li><b>Newsletter ("0stakes Insider"):</b> if you subscribe, we collect your email address. We use double opt-in, so you must confirm by email before you are added.</li>
</ul>
<p><b>Information collected automatically</b></p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Server and device data:</b> when you visit, our hosting provider and our service providers may receive your IP address, browser type and version, device type, operating system, referring page, the pages you request, and the date and time of requests. This is standard for any website and is used to deliver the site and keep it secure.</li>
  <li><b>Cookies and similar technologies:</b> see sections 2 and 3 below.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  The games run in your browser. Individual rounds and bets are never sent to us. Without
  an account, nothing about your play is sent to us. With an account, only the net result of a
  session is saved to your chip ledger. Chips are play money: they have no cash value and
  cannot be bought, sold, or cashed out. We do not ask for or collect payment information, and we
  do not sell anything on this site.
</p>

<h2>2. Cookies and local storage</h2>
<p>
  Cookies are small files stored on your device. Local storage is a similar browser feature.
  We use them as follows:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Preferences:</b> the games may save a setting, such as "fast mode", in your browser's local storage. It stays on your device and is not sent to us.</li>
  <li><b>Sign-in:</b> if you log in, your browser's local storage holds a session token from our authentication provider so you stay signed in. Logging out removes it.</li>
  <li><b>Advertising and consent:</b> Google and its partners use cookies and similar technologies for advertising and to remember your consent choices (see section 3).</li>
  <li><b>Newsletter and forms:</b> our newsletter provider may set cookies or load scripts when the signup form is displayed or used.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings. Blocking some cookies may
  affect how parts of the site (including ads and signup forms) work.
</p>

<h2>3. Advertising (Google AdSense)</h2>
<p>
  We use <b>Google AdSense</b> to show ads, which helps keep 0stakes free. Google, as a
  third-party vendor, uses cookies and similar technologies to serve ads based on your
  prior visits to this site and other sites on the internet. Google's use of advertising
  cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visit to 0stakes
  and/or other sites. In the course of serving ads, Google and its partners may collect
  your IP address, browser and device information, and information about the ads you view
  or click.
</p>
<ul>
  <li>You can opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>.</li>
  <li>You can also opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalized advertising at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a>, or through the <a href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org" rel="noopener">Network Advertising Initiative opt-out page</a>.</li>
  <li>To learn how Google uses information from sites that use its services, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>, and Google's <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
  <li>If you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or Switzerland, ads and related cookies are shown according to the choices you make in our consent message. You can change your choice at any time using the privacy settings control, where available, or by clearing this site's cookies.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  We do not control the cookies set by Google or other advertisers. Their handling of
  your information is governed by their own privacy policies.
</p>

<h2>4. How we use information</h2>
<ul>
  <li>To operate, maintain, secure, and improve the site and its games and articles.</li>
  <li>To show a public leaderboard: if you have an account, your username and chip totals (current balance and today's net game winnings) can appear on the <a href="/leaderboard/">leaderboard</a>, which anyone can see. Your email address is never shown. Choose a username that does not identify you.</li>
  <li>To run accounts: signing you in, keeping your chip balance, sending confirmation and password reset emails, and preventing abuse of the chip system.</li>
  <li>To read and respond to your messages, feedback, and requests.</li>
  <li>To send the newsletter, if you subscribed (you can unsubscribe at any time).</li>
  <li>To show advertising and measure how it performs.</li>
  <li>To detect and prevent spam, abuse, and security problems.</li>
  <li>To comply with legal obligations.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  <b>Legal bases (EEA, UK):</b> we process information with your consent (newsletter,
  advertising cookies), to respond to your requests (contact and feedback), and for our
  legitimate interests in running and securing the site.
</p>

<h2>5. Who we share information with</h2>
<p>We do not sell your personal information for money. We share information only with service providers that help us run 0stakes, and only as needed:</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Cloudflare:</b> website hosting, content delivery, and security. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare's Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
  <li><b>Supabase:</b> stores accounts, chip balances, and the chip ledger, and handles sign-in and account emails. See <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Supabase's Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
  <li><b>Google (AdSense):</b> advertising, as described in section 3.</li>
  <li><b>Formspree:</b> processes feedback form submissions. See <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener">Formspree's Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
  <li><b>MailerLite:</b> manages newsletter subscriptions and email delivery. See <a href="https://www.mailerlite.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="noopener">MailerLite's Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  We may also disclose information if required by law, to protect our rights, safety, or
  the site, or in connection with a business transfer. We never share your email address
  with advertisers.
</p>

<h2>6. How long we keep information</h2>
<p>
  We keep feedback and email correspondence only as long as needed to respond and for
  reasonable record keeping. Newsletter addresses are kept until you unsubscribe. Account information and chip history are kept until you ask us to delete your account, at which point they are removed. Server
  logs and advertising data are retained by our providers according to their own schedules.
  You can ask us to delete your information at any time (see section 8).
</p>

<h2>7. Your choices</h2>
<ul>
  <li><b>Account:</b> you can stop using your account at any time, and you can ask us to delete it and its chip history (see section 8). You can reset a forgotten password from the <a href="/account/">account page</a>.</li>
  <li><b>Newsletter:</b> use the unsubscribe link in any email, or write to us.</li>
  <li><b>Cookies and ads:</b> adjust your browser settings, use the opt-out links in section 3, or use the consent control where shown.</li>
  <li><b>Global Privacy Control:</b> where required by law, we honor opt-out preference signals such as Global Privacy Control with respect to advertising choices offered through Google's tools.</li>
</ul>

<h2>8. Your privacy rights</h2>
<p>
  Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, or
  receive a copy of your personal information, to object to or restrict certain
  processing, to withdraw consent at any time, and to lodge a complaint with your local
  data protection authority.
</p>
<p>
  <b>California and other US states.</b> Residents of California, Colorado, Connecticut,
  Virginia, Texas, and other states with privacy laws may have the right to know what
  personal information is collected, to request deletion or correction, and to opt out of
  the "sale" or "sharing" of personal information for cross-context behavioral
  advertising. We do not sell personal information for money. Advertising cookies from
  Google may count as "sharing" under some state laws, and you can opt out using the
  links in section 3 or the privacy choices control where shown. We will not discriminate
  against you for exercising your rights.
</p>
<p>
  To make a request, including deleting your account, email <a href="mailto:info@0stakes.com">info@0stakes.com</a> from the address on the account with
  the subject "Privacy request". We may need to verify your identity before acting on it,
  and we will respond within the time required by applicable law.
</p>

<h2>9. Children's privacy</h2>
<p>
  0stakes covers casino games and is intended for adults. It is not directed to children
  under 18, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone under 13
  (or the applicable minimum age in your country). Accounts are for adults 18 and over. If you believe a child has given us
  personal information, contact us and we will delete it.
</p>

<h2>10. Security</h2>
<p>
  The site is served over HTTPS and we use reputable providers, but no method of
  transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
</p>

<h2>11. International transfers</h2>
<p>
  We and our service providers may process information in the United States and other
  countries that may have different data protection laws from your own. Where required,
  providers rely on recognized safeguards for such transfers.
</p>

<h2>12. Links to other sites</h2>
<p>
  The site may link to third-party websites, including help resources and advertisers. We
  are not responsible for their content or privacy practices, so please read their policies.
</p>

<h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>
  We may update this policy from time to time. The effective date above shows when it
  was last revised. If we add services that change how we handle your information, such
  as analytics, we will update this page.
</p>

<h2>14. Contact us</h2>
<p>
  Questions or requests about this policy: <a href="mailto:info@0stakes.com">info@0stakes.com</a>
  or visit our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
</p>
